  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"Kestrel Bay Packaging Corp. grew revenue over the year, but earnings and margins declined. The most important change is that the bank calculates the Total Leverage Ratio at {{fact:e7c6b39a-e868-4737-a6fc-76c468a363cf}} against a maximum of {{fact:1ee786fb-b461-4549-a2b7-db006389a4f4}}, a breach at September 30, 2026. The compliance certificate reports {{fact:ec15fc1e-2bdd-4b2e-9347-dfc5042bdd4d}} and claims compliance. This mismatch has been escalated to committee, and the committee's handling of the breach is the decision outstanding.\"},{\"section\":\"performance\",\"body\":\"Trailing revenue rose to {{fact:a5f1430e-998a-4393-8ea3-829f9fe28f26}} from {{fact:14a616e7-164b-4454-9043-a782b89f8b9e}}, growth of {{fact:4a384374-13e4-4ad5-92df-70f1e5c40fd7}}. EBITDA fell to {{fact:1ce18cd7-79e6-40f2-a528-db6d4091791f}} from {{fact:275e0a13-54ed-472a-8b90-5ca084fef81a}}, and margin narrowed to {{fact:db668803-f5f3-4744-bf1c-2b04e563d669}} from {{fact:79c7c385-b0ee-4786-8660-734134d1ca1d}}. Net income declined to {{fact:0c85d03b-f992-4070-bb52-e0f1ab60623b}} from {{fact:b061d1a0-2f59-408e-8430-13b197a9e83f}}. Total debt edged down to {{fact:71d20595-5e69-4f9e-a535-55132b1ea038}} from {{fact:6532144c-07a3-4e6a-8428-f200afa1906f}}. Lower EBITDA still lifted leverage to {{fact:3a58d341-6fe6-454d-8b27-ef917ee6a25a}} from {{fact:70ac73de-17fe-46c7-a25a-163c452d0af7}}. Interest coverage eased to {{fact:489caf11-bfd6-4974-a5a8-8b4b35684b98}} from {{fact:9d9203d1-ab47-4982-b452-c976bf68dba3}}. The current ratio fell to {{fact:10239c1b-e62b-498d-b5c4-bf5193b94df0}} from {{fact:46154326-e926-4dd2-a4ea-585e3db5e6d4}}. DSO was unchanged at {{fact:3160d966-5f15-4e4a-8b1d-73eb79965b6c}}, DPO lengthened to {{fact:c7a567a1-1a3c-48fc-9124-135e3d56fa9f}} from {{fact:fe308c22-609c-4d5f-a61f-f69dba836d56}}, and cash rose slightly to {{fact:72450d2c-ae4e-4f8d-af8d-21be61f33451}} from {{fact:c7fe7d7f-00b7-4f3f-94f5-5a4b9e75c356}}.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"The Total Leverage Ratio is in breach. The bank's calculation of {{fact:e7c6b39a-e868-4737-a6fc-76c468a363cf}} exceeds the {{fact:1ee786fb-b461-4549-a2b7-db006389a4f4}} maximum, a cushion of {{fact:73a0f1be-e6b3-41c8-88ab-5cec81ce5057}}. The certificate reports {{fact:ec15fc1e-2bdd-4b2e-9347-dfc5042bdd4d}} and claims compliance, which differs from the bank's figure. Reviewers should reconcile the borrower's definitions and inputs against the bank's calculation. The Current Ratio is compliant at {{fact:3813a38c-187f-4e5b-848c-4b792f920a25}} against a {{fact:ee9bd154-3746-46f2-9608-e3f2701d47fa}} minimum, a cushion of {{fact:a80ae34a-8f2a-4db5-87da-8b731aa1b389}}. The certificate matches the bank's figure at {{fact:db0a66a3-28f7-48eb-aafa-2360eeaf1638}}.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The most significant item is the critical mismatch on the Total Leverage Ratio. The bank's calculation shows a breach while the certificate reports compliance, and the item has been escalated to committee. A related medium-severity signal flags negative leverage headroom of {{fact:73a0f1be-e6b3-41c8-88ab-5cec81ce5057}}. A second medium-severity signal flags thin Current Ratio headroom of {{fact:a80ae34a-8f2a-4db5-87da-8b731aa1b389}}, so leverage and liquidity are under pressure together. A low-severity signal notes that Current Ratio headroom has declined in each quarter this year, with the largest drop in the September quarter.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
